                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "benefits_md": "\n  - **Financial Assistance:** ₹20,38,000/- per village for infrastructure gap filling and development activities.  - **Infrastructure Development:** Support for roads, drinking water, sanitation, education, health, and livelihood infrastructure.  - **Village Development Plan (VDP):** Preparation and execution of need-based development plans for selected villages.  - **Convergence Support:** Integration with existing Central and State schemes to maximize development impact.  - **Awards And Incentives:** ₹5,00,000/- per village at State level for best performing villages and ₹10,00,000/- per village at National level for top selected villages.\n<br>\n\n",
          "briefDescription": "The scheme aims to develop selected villages with significant Scheduled Tribe population into model villages by providing basic infrastructure and improving socio-economic conditions.",
          "detailedDescription": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "The scheme \"Pradhan Mantri Adi Adarsh Gram Yojana (PMAAGY)\" by the Ministry Of Tribal Affairs, Government Of India, aims to transform villages with high Scheduled Tribe population into model villages through providing financial assistance for infrastructure gap filling and socio-economic development to the tribal communities. The scheme focuses on villages having at least 50% ST population. It supports the preparation and implementation of Village Development Plans. Funds are utilized for critical infrastructure gaps not covered under other schemes. Convergence with other Central and State schemes is encouraged for holistic development."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "type": "align_justify"
            },
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ""
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ],
          "detailedDescription_md": "The scheme &amp;quot;Pradhan Mantri Adi Adarsh Gram Yojana (PMAAGY)&amp;quot; by the Ministry Of Tribal Affairs, Government Of India, aims to transform villages with high Scheduled Tribe population into model villages through providing financial assistance for infrastructure gap filling and socio-economic development to the tribal communities. The scheme focuses on villages having at least 50% ST population. It supports the preparation and implementation of Village Development Plans. Funds are utilized for critical infrastructure gaps not covered under other schemes. Convergence with other Central and State schemes is encouraged for holistic development.\n<br>\n\n",
